      "notes": [
        "https://catalog.utdallas.edu/2022/undergraduate/programs/jsom/supply-chain-management (2026-07-28 14:21:22) 3/",
        "https://catalog.utdallas.edu/2022/undergraduate/programs/jsom/supply-chain-management (2026-07-28 14:21:22) 4/",
        "A practicum experience (internship) of at least 160 working hours is required; the student has the",
        "option of zero to 3 semester credit hours, depending on the particular internship, and preference",
        "for additional electives.",
        "A community engagement experience is required; the student has the option of zero or 3 semester",
        "credit hours, depending on the particular experience, and preference for additional electives.",
        "The BS SCM degree program offers students the opportunity to focus in a specific track to obtain",
        "in-depth knowledge in a specific business area depending on their interests.",
        "Students will choose at least 9 semester credit hours from one of the following tracks. Any",
        "remaining Guided Elective hours may be used toward the required internship and community",
        "engagement experience.",
        "https://catalog.utdallas.edu/2022/undergraduate/programs/jsom/supply-chain-management (2026-07-28 14:21:22) 5/",
        "Any of the courses listed in Tracks A, B, or C, or any OPRE upper-division courses that are not part",
        "of the BS SCM major preparatory, major core, or not used in major related courses, may be used",
        "to satisfy the required hours of guided elective credit. At least 6 of the 12 semester credit hours",
        "used in the General Track must have an OPRE prefix.",
        "The courses listed above can satisfy guided elective requirements in prior BS SCM catalogs, as long",
        "as credit hours are not applied elsewhere on degree plan.",
        "Three semester credit hours of equivalent or similar upper-level courses, not applied as credit",
        "hours elsewhere on degree plan, may be used to fulfill a guided elective with advance written",
        "permission from the BS SCM Program Director.",
        "Note: Course prerequisites must be met."
